AB  - This paper proposes a lightweight, end-to-end framework for constructing an interactive world model from monocular video, aimed at addressing the challenges of scene reconstruction and dynamic adjustment for platforms such as UAVs. The core innovation of this framework lies in the integration of high-fidelity 3D reconstruction with real-time, object-level interaction capabilities. Technically, we significantly enhance the model’s geometric accuracy and detail fidelity by introducing a novel depth contrastive loss to guide the 3D reconstruction; simultaneously, a flexible editing mechanism endows users with the ability to modify object attributes such as position and pose in real-time. Experiments demonstrate that the framework exhibits significant advantages in reconstruction accuracy, editing flexibility, and computational efficiency. By enabling the efficient creation of diverse dynamic environments, this research provides a practical solution for agent simulation and training in resource-constrained environments.
