AB  - In this paper, an autonomous navigation and control method is proposed based on digital twin (DT) to resolve path conflict when two unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) move towards each other. A four-dimensional digital twin system is introduced, encompassing physical space, virtual space, application service, and data processing. To deal with a dynamic obstacle in the physical space, a collision avoidance planning algorithm is developed by combining MINCO and time elastic band (TEB) for a virtual UAV and a physical UAV. To ensure motion synchronization between the virtual UAV and the physical UAV, a bidirectional synchronization control strategy is proposed based on adaptive event-triggered model predictive control (ETMPC). Experiment results demonstrate effectiveness and superiority of the collision avoidance planning algorithm and the bidirectional synchronization control strategy.
